   "slot": "parts",
   "inputs": {
    "text": "Getting there from Meridian",
    "level": "h2",
    "id": "getting-there-from-meridian-title",
    "size": "sm"
   }
  },
  {
   "uuid": "fb030357-e78b-4e79-bb41-05ebc0c66fcc",
   "component_id": "sdc.meridian.prose",
   "parent_uuid": "7a8be11b-1470-4d11-90cb-70e3b44f8807",
   "slot": "parts",
   "inputs": {
    "body": "<p>Azur Express flies to Marrakech every day from Terminal 2. ZX 762 leaves at 10:50 and takes about 3 hours 40 minutes. Morocco's clocks change on different dates from the UK's, so check the time difference in the week you travel.</p>\n<p>The airport is about 15 minutes by road from the old city, the medina. Most riads will arrange a driver to meet you, which we recommend for a first visit. Cars cannot enter most of the medina, so the driver will hand you over to someone from the riad who walks you the last few minutes.</p>"
   }
  },
  {
