  },
  {
   "uuid": "c9aac7b1-fd94-4d04-a7b9-e9e3c5cef0d4",
   "component_id": "sdc.meridian.heading",
   "parent_uuid": "8c7bc4c6-7f24-4858-8979-cbeb92bf8329",
   "slot": "parts",
   "inputs": {
    "text": "Finding your way around the souks",
    "level": "h2",
    "id": "finding-your-way-around-the-souks-title",
    "size": "sm"
   }
  },
  {
   "uuid": "2471907a-cd04-4e06-9d89-3567366f712c",
   "component_id": "sdc.meridian.prose",
   "parent_uuid": "8c7bc4c6-7f24-4858-8979-cbeb92bf8329",
   "slot": "parts",
   "inputs": {
    "body": "<p>The souks are the covered markets north of the main square. Lanes are narrow, twist constantly and change name without warning. That is part of the fun.</p>\n<ul><li>Download an offline map before you go. Mobile signal is patchy under the roofs.</li><li>Use the main square as your anchor. Most lanes eventually lead back to it.</li><li>If you are lost, ask a shopkeeper rather than someone who approaches you. People who offer to guide you will expect payment.</li><li>Mopeds use the lanes too. Keep to the side.</li></ul>\n<h3>Haggling</h3>\n<p>Prices in the souks are not fixed. Start at about half the first price, stay friendly, and be ready to walk away. Once you agree a price, it is polite to buy.</p>"
   }
  },
