  {
   "uuid": "21cefa57-d20b-43ed-b234-2bfc02859d2e",
   "component_id": "sdc.meridian.heading",
   "parent_uuid": "eaaeea12-e087-4a0f-94a0-c2636ed47ebe",
   "slot": "parts",
   "inputs": {
    "text": "See",
    "level": "h2",
    "id": "see-title",
    "size": "sm"
   }
  },
  {
   "uuid": "d03a1435-d410-4db9-8bd2-094df40523e3",
   "component_id": "sdc.meridian.prose",
   "parent_uuid": "eaaeea12-e087-4a0f-94a0-c2636ed47ebe",
   "slot": "parts",
   "inputs": {
    "body": "<ul><li><strong>The rooftops.</strong> Many cafés and riads have roof terraces. Go at sunset, when the call to prayer echoes across the city.</li><li><strong>The palaces and the old Quranic school.</strong> Tiled courtyards, carved cedar and painted ceilings. Go early to avoid the crowds.</li><li><strong>The gardens.</strong> Shady, walled gardens outside the medina make a cool break in the afternoon.</li></ul>"
   }
  },
  {
